{
  "manifest": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "body": "# Strategy probability opportunity calibration \u2014 strict 42-fold audit",
        "id": "title",
        "layout": "full",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "cardIds": [
          "conditions_card",
          "scored_folds_card",
          "brier_card",
          "logloss_card"
        ],
        "id": "metrics",
        "layout": "full",
        "type": "metric-strip"
      },
      {
        "body": "## The calibration mechanism does not clear its evidence gate\n\nThe prior-fold policy is **rejected before strategy integration**. Across 34 scored folds and 498 equally weighted terminal conditions, market-minus-calibrated Brier improvement is `-0.000145` and log-loss improvement is `+0.000017`. The first/second-half Brier improvements are `-0.001496` / `+0.001174`; log-loss improvements are `-0.003417` / `+0.003369`. No calibration coefficient should be added to strategy runtime code.",
        "id": "verdict",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "opportunity_audit",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "chartId": "cumulative_brier",
        "id": "brier_chart",
        "layout": "half",
        "type": "chart"
      },
      {
        "chartId": "cumulative_logloss",
        "id": "logloss_chart",
        "layout": "half",
        "type": "chart"
      },
      {
        "body": "## A+ remains blocked by distributed support and loss clustering\n\nThe retained volatility-floor `0.30` strategy remains profitable at measured latency: 102 trades, 79W/23L, `$+13.54` PnL, and Wilson lower `0.6843`. It still has only 19 profitable reports out of 39, a five-report loss burst of 4, and `$-4.34` in the last 21 folds. The unchanged A+ gates require Wilson at least 0.70, at least 20 profitable reports, and loss burst at most two.",
        "id": "baseline",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "strict_baseline",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Scope, data, and definitions\n\nThe harness records the first candidate per condition and UTC second only after all non-edge gates pass and before EV, stale-edge, and minimum-edge checks. Capture runs use an impossible edge threshold and fail if any order is submitted. The source manifests are complete for all 42 disjoint folds at 202 ms. Repeated seconds share one terminal label, so each condition receives total weight one.",
        "id": "scope",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "opportunity_audit",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "id": "quality",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "quality_table",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Methodology\n\nScoring starts after eight prior folds. For every scored fold, identity, market-intercept, and bounded market-to-model logit shrinkage compete on the final two strictly prior folds across a fixed ridge grid. The winner is refit on all prior folds and applied once to the next fold. Eligibility requires positive Brier and log-loss improvement overall and in both chronological halves, positive lower bounds from a 2,000-draw condition bootstrap, at least 30 scored folds, and at least 300 scored conditions.",
        "id": "methodology",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "opportunity_audit",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "id": "models",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "model_table",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Limitations and robustness\n\nThis cohort tests probability quality only within the current strategy's post-gate opportunity set; it does not discover signals outside that grammar. Bootstrap intervals are clustered by terminal condition but do not create new market regimes. The 95% intervals for market-minus-calibrated Brier and log loss are `[-0.002039189044594095, 0.0016996963068833775]` and `[-0.005735544869003813, 0.005620249899879944]`. Even a calibration pass would still need fold-specific exact L2 replay, unchanged fees and latency, and fresh fully resolved data before it could affect the A+ verdict.",
        "id": "limitations",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "opportunity_audit",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Next steps\n\n1. Keep live trading off and preserve the retained volatility-floor strategy as research-only.\n2. If calibration is rejected, do not add a runtime coefficient; use the segment evidence only to define the next independently testable mechanism.\n3. If calibration is eligible, materialize strictly prior-fitted coefficients per fold and run exact executable replay before any registry change.\n4. Require the newest fully resolved joint CLOB, Binance-signal, and Chainlink-settlement window for any future promotion decision.",
        "id": "next",
        "layout": "full",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Further questions\n\n- Does a new causal feature explain the remaining loss cluster without reducing support below 80 trades?\n- Can fresh-window capture accumulate enough fully warmed conditions to distinguish candidate mechanisms?\n- Is the apparent low-price probability degradation stable under a separately preregistered fold-forward test, given that prior minimum-price guards failed exact generalization?",
        "id": "questions",
        "layout": "full",
        "type": "markdown"
      }
    ],
